In our previous investigation using magnetometry it was inferred that TbFe0.5Mn0.5O3 orders in AxGyCz (Γ1) structure at TN[Fe][/][Mn] ≈ 286 K followed by a spin re-orientation at TSR[Fe][/][Mn] ≈ 28 K to the structure GxAyFz (Γ4)[23] . No signature of Tb ordering was obtained in the previous study. In the present manuscript, we make a detailed investigation of the magnetic structures and spin re-orientation transitions in TbFe0.5Mn0.5O3 using neutron powder diffraction in order to confirm the magnetic structure arrived at through macroscopic magnetization earlier. We update the magnetic structures as a function of temperature and observe that they evolve between Γ1 and Γ4 through mixed-domains of (Γ1 + Γ4). 

