If the two-phase layer system is not perfectly ordered ( _i.e._ , fluctuations of intercrystalline spacings, varying lamellae thicknesses, and diffuse interfaces),  W(P) exhibits a characteristic shape that is similar to a damped sine wave.[7] Various features of the characteristic shape correspond to the average amorphous layer thickness (/^) and the long period spacing (/_). The average lamella thickness (/?) is the difference between /_ and /^. 

The arbitrary intensity units of the SAXS patterns reported in this manuscript prevent direct calculation of W(P). Instead, each semi-crystalline PE- _g_ , PE- _v_ , and insoluble portion of PE- _v_ SAXS pattern was converted into a non-absolute unit electron density correlation function, `(P) using the equation 

