where +(C) is the SAXS scattering pattern intensity in arbitrary units. Despite the use of arbitrary units, `(P) has the same characteristic shape and horizontal positioning as W(P), so determination /^, /_, and /? is the same. 

Figure S21A displays the estimated `(P) curves for neat PE. The curve peak corresponded to an /_ value of 21 ± 1 nm. /^ was found by finding the intersection between the `(P) minimum and X`/XP, which is an extrapolation of the linear portion of the curve near P = 0. /^ was estimated to be 4 ± 1 nm. Accordingly, /? was 16 ± 2 nm. 

