## **III. CHARACTERIZATION** 

Backscatter X-ray Laue diffraction was performed as a preliminary investigation of the crystallinity and orientation of the material (Fig. 3). Based on a changing diffraction pattern during translation, we were able to identify grain boundaries. Through systematic scanning and slicing, the polycrystal was cut into a rectangular prism of dimensions 3.4 mm x 3.3 mm x 3.0 mm while mapping the crystal orientation of the polycrystalline sample. The final product was polycrystalline with the (100) direction of the dominant grain along one face of the rectangular prism. Fig. 3 shows a Laue pattern for the dominant grain, demonstrating the archetypal 4-fold symmetry of the cubic lattice along the (100) direction. 

Magnetic susceptibility measurements were performed using a Quantum Design MPMS 5 Superconducting Quantum Interference Device (SQUID) with an AC option installed. The high temperature ferromagnetic phase was verified via field cooling (FC) from 400 K (Fig. 4). The onset of the transition was found to be 320 K, consistent with Ref. [27]. A Curie-Weiss fit between 350 K and 400 K results in an effective magnetic moment of 1.6 _µB_ , consistent with the magnetic moment found for other Co _x_ Zn _y_ Mn _z_ (x+y+z=20) compounds [41]. The 

