The mechanism of formation of SLC16:0 fibers undergoes a continuous micelle-tofiber transition, characterized by a morphological evolution of the micelles. When the pH decreases, the hydrophilic shell becomes more homogeneous in the equatorial direction, most likely due to the increasing amount of carboxylic acids. Micelles then fuse together both in the equatorial and polar directions, probably through H-bonding interactions, with a 

