## Document

Evidence of nickel ions dimerization in NiWO4 and NiWO4 –ZnWO4 solid solutions probed by EXAFS spectroscopy and reverse Monte Carlo simulations 

Georgijs Bakradze[a,] _[∗]_ , Aleksandr Kalinko[a] , Alexei Kuzmin[a] 

> _aInstitute of Solid State Physics, University of Latvia, 8 Kengaraga street, Riga LV-1063, Latvia_ 

## **Abstract** 

The existence of exchange-coupled Ni[2+] ions – the so-called magnetic dimers – in wolframite-type NiWO4 and Zn _c_ Ni1– _c_ WO4 solid solutions with high nickel content was discovered by X-ray absorption spectroscopy combined with reverse Monte Carlo (RMC) simulations. Temperature- (10–300 K) and composition-dependent x-ray absorption spectra were measured at the Ni K- edge, Zn K-edge, and W L3-edge of microcrystalline NiWO4, Zn _c_ Ni1– _c_ WO4 and ZnWO4. Structural models were obtained from simultaneous analysis of the extended x-ray absorption fine structure (EXAFS) spectra at three metal absorption edges using RMC simulations. The obtained radial distribution functions for different atomic pairs made it possible to trace in detail the changes in the local environment of metal ions and the effect of thermal disorder. Dimerization of Ni[2+] ions within quasi-one-dimensional zigzag chains of [NiO6] octahedra was evidenced in NiWO4 in the whole studied temperature range. It manifests itself as the splitting of the Ni–Ni radial distribution 

