## **PNR Fitting Considerations and Model Development** 

PNR is a powerful nondestructive technique that allows evaluation of both structural and magnetic 

2 

## **Supporting Information** 

changes along the sample thickness. Real space information is inferred from model fitting of the PNR data.  As such, care must be taken to ensure that the data actually provides sensitivity to parameters of interest.  For this reason, it is important to start with the simplest case and evolve it towards a more complex model that makes physical sense. In the present system it is important to use this sequence of fits to justify inclusions like the ferromagnetic (FM) interfacial layers, track oxygen distribution throughout Gd, and to avoid inclusion of layers in our model that the data do not actually provide sensitivity to. In the following section, some of the tested models used to converge on a solution and proper model determination will be described. 

