## **4.3 The double counting parameter** _µ_ dc 

As stated above, the bare energy of the Ce 4f states is obtained from the GGA value by subtracting the doublecounting correction _µ_ dc, which accounts for the Ce 4 _f_ –4 _f_ interaction that is already present in the GGA description. In practice, _µ_ dc renormalizes the energy splitting between the Ce 4 _f_ states and Pd 4 _d_ (and other) bands, which is illustrated in Supplementary Fig. 5. As a consequence, the position of the 4 _f_[2] peak (at around 5 eV in the experimental data) is sensitive to _µ_ dc, despite a small change in the Ce 4 _f_ occupation ( _N_ 4 _f_ in the figure). This allows us to fix _µ_ dc _≈−_ 2 _._ 25 eV. 

Aside from these valence spectra (Supplementary Fig. 5), the obtained Ce 4 _f_ self-energies Σ( _ε_ ) are also highly sensitive to _µ_ dc, as discussed below in the context of Supplementary Fig. 6. 

