The inset of Fig. 4(a) shows a magnified view of the pre-edge region. Although the K-edge XAS reflects mostly the transitions to unoccupied Co 4p states, M.C. Lee et al. showed that the pre-edge anomalies α and β1 are related to Co 4p partial electron filling via intrasite mixing with Co 3d orbitals [12]. Thus, the orbital hybridization with Ir 5d orbitals may largely contribute to these pre-edge features (see Fig. 6). Interestingly, a third anomaly, β2 ∼ 7720 eV, is observed for Ca0.5 and Ba0.5, which may be related to Co[3+] (3d eg ⊕ 4p) – Ir 5d eg hybridization via O 2p. 

