## **Calculation of grafting density** 

To determine the grafting density of PNIPAM on the AuNPs, we consider the scenario where PNIPAM3k-AuNPs have completely collapsed, releasing any trapped water. In this state, the overall diameter of the combined nanoparticle closely aligns with _d_ NN. By measuring the difference in volume (∆ _V_ ) between the bare AuNP ( _D_ calculated from form factor measurements) and this combined structure, we can deduce the volume occupied by the grafted PNIPAM. This, in turn, can be employed to compute the weight of the attached PNIPAM ( _W_ PNIPAM) and, subsequently, the number of grafted chains per AuNP. 

