**Electron Microscopy.** Energy Dispersive X-ray Spectroscopy (EDS) mappings were obtained using a BRUKER XFlash 6160 system, while microstructure analysis was performed with a ZEISS GEMINI field emission scanning electron microscope (FE-SEM). High-angle annular dark-field scanning transmission electron microscopy (HAADF-STEM) was conducted using a JEOL ARM-200F microscope with cold FEG probe image aberration correction at 200 kV to investigate the crystal structure. All measurements were conducted at room temperature. 

**Raman Spectra.** Raman spectra were collected from powdered samples under ambient conditions using a LabRAM HR Raman spectrometer (Horiba, France) with a 532 nm laser source. 

In the present paper, we have synthesized a new series of Cr-based low, medium, and high entropy spinel oxides having compositions NiCr2O4, [Ni0 _._ 5Mn0 _._ 5]Cr2O4, [Ni0 _._ 33Mn0 _._ 33Co0 _._ 33]Cr2O4, [Ni0 _._ 25Mn0 _._ 25Co0 _._ 25Cu0 _._ 25]Cr2O4, [Ni0 _._ 2Mn0 _._ 2Co0 _._ 2Cu0 _._ 2Zn0 _._ 2]Cr2O4, and [Ni0 _._ 2Mg0 _._ 2Co0 _._ 2Cu0 _._ 2Zn0 _._ 2]Cr2O4 by systematically increasing the configuration entropy (and chemical complexity) in the A site of the Cr-based spinel structure. We have presented detailed and systematic structural (using X-ray powder diffraction, neutron powder diffraction, and electron microscopy), magnetic (magnetization), Raman spectroscopy, and X-ray absorption spectroscopy 

