The magnetic contribution was isolated by subtracting the instrumental background and nuclear contributions of _S_ ( **Q** _, ω_ ) measured at _µ_ 0 _H_ = 0 T and 5 K. A cut through the magnetic excitations, _S_ ( _ω_ ) integrated across 0.5 _< ξ <_ 1.0, is shown in Figs. 2 (b,d,f,h) to present clearly the field dependence of the peak positions, linewidths and any further broad scattering features. 

Fig. 2(a,b), _S_ ( **Q** _, ω_ ) and _S_ ( _ω_ ) for _µ_ 0 _H_ = 0 T, shows an inelastic nearly dispersionless contribution at ∆ _E_ = 0.02(1) and 0.096(2) meV (INS1,INS2) and a further nearly dispersionless excitation at 0.7 meV (INS3), consistent with previous results [9, 20]. In Fig. 

