## **Supplementary Fig. 4. Raman spectrum of the post-impact recovered magnesiosiderite crystal** 

**shows a magnesiosiderite-hematite mix.** Extensive mapping of the crater floor (e.g., Supplementary Fig. 3) in the post-impact recovered magnesiosiderite crystals show a few rare crystallites of hematite, Fe2O3. The bands at 222, 412, and 1318 cm[-1 ] are assigned to hematite [72]. Hematite also has a band at 612 cm[-1 ] [72], which is likely encompassed in the broad band at 660 cm[-] 1. While magnetite (Fe3O4) also has a band at ∼660 cm-1 [63], the appearance of the band at this position in our spectrum cannot be conclusively attributed to magnetite. 

