**Supplementary Fig. 5. Error in pressure.** Multiple shots were performed at the same laser intensity. Pressure values were calculated using the VISAR data and the method described in section II-C of the main text. The largest variation in the value of measured particle velocity ( _up_ ), and hence the pressure, is used as the error value for all pressure points. This largest variation in _up_ occurs at the laser intensity of 2.3 x 10[12 ] W cm[-2 ] (Supplementary Fig. 7), and gives a value of ±15 GPa as the error in pressure. 

