To accurately simulate the dipole field at the muon stopping site, muon-induced crystallographic distortions were incorporated following Ref. [S33]. These distortions slightly cant the field out of the _ab_ -plane (as the _c_ -axis components no longer perfectly cancel), consistent with the small oscillating asymmetry observed in the forwardbackward detector pair. We assumed an equal population of all magnetic domains across all calculations. While other reasonable assumptions (e.g., unequal domain populations or the presence of domain walls) would slightly modify the calculated dipole fields (particularly the ratio between the high and low fields and their relative weightings) these subtle variations do not alter our fundamental conclusions. 

