## **IV. MnTe2 IMPURITY** 

The sample discussed throughout the main text (sample A) was grown via the Bridgman technique. The samples primarily discussed below in this Supplemental Material (samples B and C) were grown using a Te-rich selfflux method, following the procedure detailed in Ref. [S4]. This yielded high-quality platelike single crystals with lateral dimensions of several millimeters and thicknesses of several hundred micrometers. The crystallographic _c_ axis is oriented normal to the plate surface. 

Scanning electron microscopy (SEM) revealed MnTe2 impurities in all samples. In the Bridgman-grown crystal (sample A), MnTe2 appeared as precipitates aligned along the (0001) planes within the bulk, constituting a volume fraction below 2%. Conversely, in the flux-grown crystals (samples B and C), MnTe2 formed exclusively on 

