## 5. DISCUSSION 

We start our discussion with a question: Is a singlemode approximation sufficient to describe interatomic distances in the second Pb–Pb shell of the PbTe1−xSex solid solution? 

It has been proposed [1, 17] that the number of modes in the distribution of the A–A distances in an AB1−xCx solid solution is determined by the number of different ways that link two A atoms, i.e. the distribution should be bimodal for lattices with a zinc blende structure and trimodal for NaCl structure. 

That is why we initiated our data analysis by seeking parameters that approximate the distribution function as a sum of a few Gaussians. Unfortunately, a large Debye–Waller factor and a limited k range of EXAFS oscillations did not enable us to determine the parame- 

