## **Author contributions** 

## **Use of large language models** 

We used the large language model tools Claude (Anthropic) and Antigravity (Google) to assist with writing the analysis and reconstruction code, with the data analysis, and with drafting and editing the manuscript text. The authors reviewed, tested, and revised all output and take full responsibility for the code, the results, and the content of this article. 

## **Data and code availability** 

The measured XMCD projections, the preprocessed solver inputs, the synthetic ground truth, and every reconstruction shown in the main text and the Extended Data will be archived at Zenodo upon journal publication. The preprocessing and reconstruction code (the `xmcdrecon` package, JAX and NeuralMag), with the recipes and commands behind every measured-data reconstruction of this work, will be released on GitHub and archived at Zenodo upon journal publication. 

A.S. developed the physics-informed reconstruction framework, carried out the reconstructions and the analysis, and wrote the manuscript. P.M. prepared the samples, performed the X-ray ptychographic tomography measurements, the ptychographic reconstruction and coarse alignment of the projections, and contributed to the magnetic reconstructions and the analysis. L.J.R.H. and B.K. set up and operated beamline I08-1 and supported the ptychographic tomography measurements. L.T., R.Y., and M.R.F. contributed to the X-ray measurements. D.A.M. and G.B. grew the single crystals. A.C. contributed to the implementation of the reconstruction method. D.S. contributed to the supervision of the project. A.F.-P. and M.G.-S. contributed to the conception and planning of the project and to writing the proposal. C.D. supervised the experimental work. C.A. is the lead developer of the underlying NeuralMag micromagnetic framework and contributed to and supervised the development of the reconstruction method. All authors discussed the reconstructions, the analysis, and the results, and commented on the manuscript. 

